  "title": "Pause Before You Act",
  "description": "When faced with a problem: - Ask first: \"Is action really necessary, or is waiting better?\" - Consider the outcomes: Think about what happens if you do nothing. - Break the impulse: Take 10 deep breaths to disrupt the urge to act immediately. Example: Someone sends a critical email. Instead of replying instantly, pause and evaluate whether a response is even required.",
